# Local styx-emulator patch teaching the PowerQUICC I `mtspr` hook about the
# decrementer: it records a reload value, advances DEC/TB once per stride, and
# serves guest `mfspr DEC` / `mftb` from the SIU shadow. The MPC8xx DEC and TB
# SPRs are not visible to the Unicorn backend, so without this a guest reads
# stale backend state.
#
# This hook also owns `rfi`, restoring PC/MSR from the MPC866M controller's
# shadow SRRs - and therefore also mirrors guest `mtspr`/`mfspr SRR0/SRR1` into
# and out of that shadow, since the backend registers those writes land in are
# ones `rfi` never reads. That lives here rather than in a code hook registered by the
# controller because `CodeHook::call` is not told which address it was
# dispatched for: every whole-range hook must read `pc()` to find its own
# instruction, and the `rfi` path rewrites it, so whichever of two such hooks
# ran second would decode the return target instead. One hook that reads `pc()`
# once and dispatches on the opcode makes that unrepresentable.
#
# Cut against styx-emulator 71a7746fe192a56b257549842cc3ec55ffc8f75a
# (the `rev` pinned in ../default.nix). Touches no Cargo.toml, so the vendored
# crate set and `cargoDeps` hash are unchanged.
#
# Remove once styx-emulator models the MPC8xx decrementer upstream.
--- a/styx/processors/ppc/styx-powerquicci-processor/src/system_interface_unit/mtspr_manager.rs
